test(hydrofrac): fold the oracle tests' engine-parameterised builders

With one engine, every `*_in(check, ...)` builder in `check/brute_tests.rs` was called with
`EcCheck::new()` only (they let one program run under lite or races):

- `plain_broadcast_in`, `echo_broadcast_in` and `total_loss_masks_a_partial_loss_in` are
  merged into their wrappers;
- `lossy_relay_chain` loses its `check` argument;
- `positional_crash_order_relay` and `positional_crash_order_relay_in` become one builder
  taking `max_faults` and `max_crashes`.

No test or expectation changes.
